{"connection_id": "BC-3d5a60ae5571f4bcada3", "ref": "WLC:Ezek.23.25", "target": "sec7", "tradition": "tevrat", "kind": "motif", "basis": "nose and ears cut; survivors consumed by fire", "note": "In the allegory of Jerusalem and Samaria's infidelity, enemies mutilate the women's faces and the remnant is consumed by fire; it supplies a concrete judgment-image of facial stigma joined to fire, while the context and instrument differ from the commentary's brand."}
